@nsobid-FF1D1C05670DB6021C85B624A710B963

# Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass.
//
// All of the game's AA is agl::pfx::FilterAA, drawn at the end of the gsys
// final-image pass (sub_7103939550). It dispatches on an antialias_type that
// scene settings can change: 0 = FXAA (with history reprojection), 1 =
// ReduceAA, 2 = SMAA, 3 = a draw callback.
//
// Whether the filter runs is one test: the scene allows AA, the filter's scale
// is above zero, and the filter is enabled. It is made twice: the view setup
// (sub_710393787C) asks for the scene's AA render target when it passes, and
// the final-image pass routes the image through the filter. Both copies now
// take their false result, so the scene renders straight to the final target as
// it does when a scene turns the filter off, and no AA mode runs whatever
// antialias_type, enable flag or scale is set.

@enabled
039378E0 E8031F2A   // MOV W8,WZR: view setup never requests the AA target (was CSEL W8,W8,WZR,NE)
039395B0 06000014   // B to the AA-off result in the final-image pass (was LDR S0,[X21,#0xE30] = FilterAA scale)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3 (sead
// + agl/gsys, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located
// by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
